WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.192
The Neural Tangent Kernel has become a powerful
tool for understanding neural networks

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.671
with infinitely many hidden nodes.

00:00:08.751 --> 00:00:14.651
It has been derived for multi-layer perceptrons,
convolutional networks, and more,

00:00:14.731 --> 00:00:17.422
each yielding its own distinct kernel.

00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:20.995
But no one had derived an NTK for tree ensembles.

00:00:21.075 --> 00:00:25.517
Because soft trees inherit characteristics of
neural networks,

00:00:25.597 --> 00:00:29.455
the authors saw the NTK framework as the natural lens,

00:00:29.535 --> 00:00:33.830
seeking a closed-form kernel for infinitely many
soft trees.
